module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.census_rows_read_the_loaded_population

import std.types { String, NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundOnRung, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { MechanicallyPreventable, Mitigatable }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

// REGISTERED BY THE SHARD-CONTEXT DEFECT (Manager 1, 2026-10-21, msg_dfb4289f; strengthened by
// clever-carp-254's fleet rows at run 39622052948 and sunny-bee-153's artifact read on branch
// scratch/census-nonhermetic-evidence). A native census row must be a function of the MODULE and its
// CLOSURE. It is not: an unimported ambient spelling (list_push, first, contains, ...) binds iff its
// contract row sits in the symbol index of the modules the run LOADED (v2.compiler.resolve
// resolve_atom_primitive_authority), and the loaded population is the SUBJECTS' closures -- so a
// byte-identical module's ambient rows still depend on which SUBJECTS were asked. THE CLASS IS OPEN AT
// THIS HEAD: this diff changes no census behavior versus main (the acquisition already read the subjects
// exactly; it now says so at one named boundary) and records what two executed attempts proved about
// closing it. ATTEMPT ONE (#14710 as first written, 533defac4713) appended the contract module to every
// population -- executed WRONG: the census bound through contract rows the native route refuses at
// (see THE EARLIEST BOUNDARY, below). ATTEMPT TWO (#14832, closed) joined that roster onto the route too --
// executed WRONG at the source: the route began resolving list_push THROUGH a contract row, which N7
// retires (list_push's one declared home is #14751). The surviving ruling (v2 native, October 2026):
// NEITHER acquisition path admits the ambient contracts; the census matches the route for the SAME
// subject list -- which is what the identity boundary pins, byte-identical first fatals included. What
// CLOSES the class is a per-name ambient disposition from Seat 12 (never a census-only substrate), or a
// comparison run at one canonical population -- both named below as the open half; this PR lands the
// boundary they land at, not a claim of closure.

data census_rows_read_the_loaded_population: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "census_rows_read_the_loaded_population" as NonEmptyStr,

  // The rung is READABLE for this class, so it is read (review 84236 / side chat RC, October 2026;
  // rung re-read OPEN at this head per review 84904: both executed closure attempts are recorded
  // below and both were reversed, so NO repaired execution is claimed). The RED discriminates by
  // execution on the real files: on ONE binary, a byte-identical module's ambient primitive rows
  // read bound in one subject population and unbound in another (the fermi flip receipt below) --
  // the rows still depend on the loaded population whenever two runs load different populations,
  // which is the fleet's base-vs-shard comparison (1,948-module base vs 165-module shards) today.
  // CURRENT is Mitigatable, on two executed pieces: (1) WITHIN a run, the roster-home closure carry
  // (session branch ebf6504d42b9, precheck fleet run 39833573589: DOOR 21->1, READ 210->10) computes
  // the wave population ONCE and threads it into every provider, so the 21 recomputations that
  // previously could diverge are one fact -- built and prechecked, not yet merged. (2) CROSS-PATH,
  // for the SAME subject list the census now agrees with the route (executed, run IDs in the PR
  // receipt: both first fatals resolve_reason_unbound_symbol @ dag/std/algebra.dag bytes 5195..5204,
  // list_push). The OPEN face, stated plainly: a comparison ACROSS runs with different subject lists
  // -- the fleet's 1,948-module base vs 165-module shards of one tree -- still loads different
  // populations, and a byte-identical module's ambient rows can still flip between them. That face
  // closes only at Seat 12's per-name dispositions (below) or at one canonical population for the
  // comparison; this diff claims neither. CEILING is MechanicallyPreventable and the blocker
  // is unbuilt work, not a grounding: per-name ambient dispositions from Seat 12 (the surviving
  // ruling), consumed at the one boundary native_census_scoped_entries, so whether a name binds
  // stops being a function of the loaded population at all -- or, as its mechanical floor, one
  // ingest+resolve per run keyed by content identity (the same hoist that ends the ~110-minute
  // per-round re-read at the fleet's base profile). Trigger capability: the per-name disposition
  // table consulted at that boundary, executed check = one supplied-population claim per
  // dispositioned name that passes with the name UNIMPORTED in a fixture module no other subject
  // names.
  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable }, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable }, ceiling: MechanicallyPreventable, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "the per-name ambient disposition table (Seat 12's admitted dispositions) consulted at the native_census_scoped_entries boundary, so a name's binding state stops being a function of the loaded population -- executed check = one supplied-population claim per dispositioned name that passes with the name UNIMPORTED in a fixture module no other subject names; its mechanical floor, one ingest+resolve per run keyed by content identity, is checked by the fleet log's census Filesystem.Read count (once vs 10 x 22)." } },

  receipts: [
    "THE FAILURE MODE: the resolver's ambient primitive-authority tier (v2.compiler.resolve resolve_atom_primitive_authority) binds an unimported spelling -- first, contains, map_get, starts_with, join, split, replace, string_length, fold, keys, values -- by looking up a contract row (std.primitives.<name>_contract) in the symbol index of the modules the run LOADED. While the scoped census loaded exactly the named subjects' closures, whether such a name bound was a fact about the invocation's subject list, not about the module: the same module, same binary, emitted binding_partial ... ambient:primitive_authority std.primitives.first_contract in one run and binding_unbound in another, because std.primitives rode the first run's closures and not the second's. A census consumer comparing base against shards then reads the difference as a behavior change of the module and refuses a merge that changed nothing -- which is exactly how this blocked //gunbc/instruments:namespace-wave-binding-diff's positive merge for #14324.",

    "THE TELL: a binding row for a module whose bytes are byte-identical between two runs differs in binding state (partial<->unbound), the flipped names are all ambient primitive spellings, and the two runs loaded different module populations (check the census_run_comparable population field, or the run's subject list). The module's own imports are unchanged and do not name the substrate -- ambient resolution is import-free by design, which is what makes the population an invisible dependency.",

    "EXECUTED REPRODUCTION, one binary (emitted driver, sha256 2742801a..., head 3cd5c856e48f, instrument route //gunbc/instruments:v2-native-census-scoped), the subject list the ONLY variable: census-scoped //std/fermi:all prints 'binding_unbound std.fermi first 72:20' while census-scoped //std/fermi:all //std/primitives:all prints 'binding std.fermi first 0 ambient:primitive_authority std.primitives.first_contract 72:20'; the uri_path pair (//extdeps/uri_path:all plus/minus //std/primitives:all) shows the same flip on 'contains' at 82:15, aggregate binding_unbound 157 vs 58. THE FLEET ROWS (clever-carp-254, fermi/ at scratch branch 359d18ef): base tree 02b9486ad13 vs head 80fe982d7f37, std.fermi byte-identical, same instrument revision acb862a78f625330-d48b9c56c12811d2 -- exactly a 3-row delta (binding_partial first ... first_contract 72:20 + its two module-count rollups, versus binding_unbound) across base (1,948-module population) and all four shards (165 modules); the four shards agree with each other as sets. sunny-bee-153's EVIDENCE.txt: std.primitives has 0 rows in the shard population vs 374 at base, and every untouched-module difference is one of ~25 primitive spellings flipping partial->unbound.",

    "THE EARLIEST BOUNDARY (DESIGN 6b): not the resolver tier -- reading the loaded index is what a namespace lookup IS. The boundary is the ACQUISITION. THE FIRST FIX AT THAT BOUNDARY WAS EXECUTED WRONG, and the executed wrongness is the receipt: appending the contract module to every scoped population (#14710 as first written, head 533defac4713) made the census load a resolution authority the NATIVE ROUTE never loads (fn native_lane_candidate_entries had no such append). Measured on the D1 matrix (same binaries, both acquisition paths): with the append, the route's parse-label first fatal sat at resolve_reason_unbound_symbol @ dag/std/algebra.dag bytes 5195..5204 (list_push) while the substrate-fed census bound list_push THROUGH std.primitives.list_push_contract; the follow-on join (#14832, moving the roster onto the route) proved which side moves -- the route's first fatal then MOVED to Map @ bytes 73768..73771, i.e. the route began resolving list_push through a contract row, which the v2 native ruling forbids (ambient contracts retire; list_push gets its one DECLARED home, #14751). A probe showed a population entry binds ONLY contract-registry rows: adding std.types to the population left bare Map unbound (scratch/qc503-substrate-types @ 8461234f66ea). And the census claims' green was BORROWED from the append: with the roster gone the claim module itself cannot prepare, because its std.algebra import's body uses ambient list_push (probe scratch/qc503-claims-only @ 4741a1f271c9, all members refused at prepare). THE SURVIVING RULING IS THE OPPOSITE DIRECTION: neither acquisition path admits the ambient contracts -- native_census_scoped_entries returns THE SUBJECTS EXACTLY (identity, argv order, nothing appended) and the route appends nothing either. HONESTY REQUIREMENT (review 84904): the head's acquisition BEHAVIOR equals main's -- main already passed the subjects exactly; what the head adds is that the fact lives at ONE named boundary with the ruling's reasoning, that an append inside the boundary function would surface as a census-vs-route divergence at the instrument (below), and that the executed direction-measurement above is recorded where a third attempt can find it. The CLASS IS OPEN: identity makes the population a pure function of the SUBJECTS, so two runs of the SAME subject list agree (census-vs-route same-subject agreement executed: both first fatals resolve_reason_unbound_symbol @ dag/std/algebra.dag bytes 5195..5204, list_push, rows reporting list_push unbound -- run IDs in the PR receipt); two runs with DIFFERENT subject lists -- the fleet's 1,948-module base vs 165-module shards -- still load different populations and a byte-identical module's ambient rows can still flip. Closure lands at Seat 12's per-name dispositions consumed at this boundary, or at one canonical population for the comparison. NO CLAIM MODULE GUARDS THE BOUNDARY: four probe rounds (scratch/qc503-boundary-probe1 `==` over lists; probe2 `==` on bare String literals plus positional probes; probe3 positional-only matches with an import of the boundary module; probe4 a bare String equality in a module importing ONLY std.types -- refused at eval, cause=eval_rejected_grounding_not_derived) measured that no such claim executes TODAY, at main or at this head -- the same minimal module refuses identically on main (scratch/qc503-probe4-on-main @ 7b954f7182cc, cause=eval_rejected_grounding_not_derived, the claim lane's own grounding requirement, NOT an effect of this rework), so an un-executed claim here would be the decoration DESIGN section 4b forbids (and DESIGN section 5: Done means a real consumer green by execution). THE EXECUTED GUARD IS THE CENSUS/ROUTE RUN-PAIR AT ONE IDENTITY: //gunbc/instruments:v2-native-census-scoped (whose report the driver baseline-diffs via its census-run record, refusing BaselineNotCompared when the diff is unavailable) run in one dispatch beside the route's parse-label run -- the acceptance runs above ARE that pair; an append inside the boundary function shows up there as a census-side divergence in rows or first fatal against the route's. NOT closure evidence, and it does not catch a bypass at the call site or a second acquisition route (the row's open ceiling); the fleet revalidation runs carry the same pair at composed identities.",

    "THE OPEN HALF, recorded here so it is not lost: the fleet ALSO reported per-module observation flips (gunbc.host_names.gen_z and extdeps.bmc.ipmi_boot_selection reading ObservationComplete in some shard ranges and ObservationIncomplete with reason native_census_infer_stops_at_first_fatal in others, same binary). That pairing does not exist at main: the reason is minted only in the InferRefused arm of native_census_infer_completeness and cannot pair with outcome=resolve_refused, and a bisect over the shard-B subject prefix (223, 112, 56, 28, 14, 7, 3, 1 subjects, and gen_z alone) shows the printed observation never flips on any population -- so the report is an unverified transcription (its author's own caution, relayed by deep-hawk-258) or a reading of the cause-group STAGE rather than the observation field. A second population-read candidate -- the emitted walk threading context = step.context.clone() across modules (src/v1/05_emit_rust.dag) so module N resolves against module N-1's published closure -- is real as code but produced no observation flip in the bisect. NEITHER is claimed as fixed. The next rung: a fleet re-run on the fixed identity (base + shards + positive merge/4) either reproduces an observation flip -- at which point the per-module context threading becomes the suspect and its own trigger fires -- or retires the report; the per-round census re-ingest measured by clever-carp-254 (22 clusters x ~5m07s in the binding-diff walk, population-independent) is the same open half's cost face and stays open until the round count in a fleet log drops to one ingest of the shared closure.",

    "THE COST, one sentence: one full positive-merge chain (#14324) plus three sessions' fleet hours went into bisecting a 'behavior change' in a module whose bytes never changed, while the only variable -- the subject list -- sat outside the census record's comparison.",

    "THE PHASE MARKERS are gone: run_namespace_wave_binding_diff and its seed-growth justification were retired with the binding diff (retire-by-default, gunbc#15415).",

    "THE EXECUTED RECEIPT THAT BLOCKS EVERY SCOPED CENSUS (calm-ferret-416, D13 whole-pool cost lane): two preconditions before the dependency-demand census can adopt module_acquisition acquire_census_closure_of. (1) THE ACQUISITION'S MEMBER FRONT END RUNS THE PRODUCTION LOWERING WITHOUT demand_census_strip: the emitted driver verb `census-scoped //gunbc/board_authority_binding:all` returns NativeCensusScopeBlocked at the entry, CensusMemberFrontEndRefused, body_lowering_reason_uses_clause_unmodeled at the uses clause, so every uses-fn declarer is blocked at acquisition and never reaches resolve; the demand-census verb strips between parse and normalize and reads the same file (0 file refusals). (2) THE AMBIENT CLASS ON THE ACQUIRED CLOSURE: `census-scoped //std/algebra:all` over dag and src/v2 closes NativeCensusScopeClosed with 4 members (std.algebra, std.optional, std.error_primitives, std.float), and census-resolve on that closure still refuses std.algebra, 44 resolve_reason_unbound_symbol and 17 resolve_anonymous_record_no_expected_type: `list_push` (a pipeline spelling, first at L180) and the type `Map` (first at L265; std.types declares it and std.algebra never imports std.types) bind only from the loaded population. std.algebra is the hub, 46 modules fan out from it. A narrowed ingest therefore refuses where the full pool resolves, so closure rows would differ from full-ingest rows. ATTRIBUTION OF THE FULL-POOL 0-OF-210 is NOT this row's class: fleet run 39769560992 (instrument-dispatch, dependency-demand-census) carries per-row reasons, 147 module_resolve_refused (121 declarer_refused, 26 unbound), 60 importee_refused, 3 file_refused, i.e. the v2 front-end coverage cascade; the census cost there (about 250 ms per file in the per-file fold, linear) is a separate follow-up.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
